Recent review notes
- Rechecked all listed repository tips on 2026-11-27 10:50 UTC. The local
  NVIDIA branch now includes experimental DLSS Super Resolution at
  e6f8adac2079.
- cool_fox added a per-lane retry when wave-wide SCC lowering refuses a
  shader. It can keep a dispatch from being dropped, but is explicitly
  inexact; the retry and shader-cache variant changes are not ported pending
  title-shader correctness validation.
- runkmaskin added a persistent parallel shader-precompile queue and broad
  translator/emitter changes, claiming 30-40% less CPU per shader with
  byte-identical DXIL. Promising for preload time, but not ported pending
  independent benchmark and translator regression testing.
- Androtim/MiniVI advanced by 135 commits in a broad cool_fox/low-VRAM merge.
  Too many coupled renderer, shader, memory and loader changes for a safe
  bulk port.
- Bebrik's latest commit finalizes an ambient march clamp and opt-in hair
  pass; rhythmhere's latest changes include 6 GB-targeted rendering changes
  and different ambient/pipeline settings in its RTX 4050 launcher. Keep
  these profiles opt-in and target-validated; no changes imported.
- Zaxix's two newer commits are performance-audit documentation only.
- whiteh4cker-tr's new tip includes the previously noted BC7, raw-view,
  helper-priority, descriptor-lifetime, ambient-probe and Bink changes; its
  latest commit is primarily launcher/documentation. No changes imported.
- trustno1-coder's earlier declared-DXBC-extent fix is already ported locally
  in apps/victory/src/shader.rs with focused extent tests.
- trustno1-coder and Androtim added BC7 rotation-mode correction, raw buffer
  view bounds handling, and helper-thread priority changes. trustno1 also has
  descriptor-heap ownership/lifetime fixes, ambient-probe cleanup, and an
  opt-in Bink skip. Review candidates; none ported in this scan.
- cool_fox added EXEC preservation for stores behind wave-wide SCC branches,
  with shader regression tests. Potential shader-correctness candidate; not
  ported pending review against this branch's shader lowering.
- rhythmhere added direct NGX DLSS Super Resolution plus Streamline DLSS-G,
  frame tagging, and a menu. The RTX 3060 may use DLSS SR, but DLSS-G is not
  a target for this GPU. The integration spans SDK loading, resource/list
  handling, and presentation; treat as a reference, not a safe cherry-pick.
- runkmaskin added broad async HLE/scatter-map and memory bookkeeping changes;
  not ported pending targeted review.
- Bebrik229's 22-commit advance contains broad host/readback/memory lifetime
  work and enables additional performance knobs. Not a safe bulk port; target
  validation is needed.
- Zaxix added early compute-pipeline creation and drop-reason accounting;
  review separately before considering it for startup stalls.
- stellarr-studio corrected its open-world benchmark interpretation in README;
  no runtime changes in this update.
- The placed-copy RT ordering/forwarding path is already present here and
  opt-in. The player's initial A/B report: slightly better, not revolutionary.
- RTX 50 frame generation is not applicable to the RTX 3060. DualSense HID
  is unrelated to rendering.
- fxceless's ray-tracing builder changes span memory tracking and shader paths;
  the current NVIDIA play set keeps that builder path disabled.
- Dolberthi's earlier performance commit spans pool sizing, descriptors,
  indirect execution, synchronization, shader lowering and loader hooks; not
  a safe single-change port.
